<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD JATS (Z39.96) Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v1.0 20120330//EN" "JATS-archivearticle1.dtd"><article xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Int J Emerg Med</journal-id><journal-title-group><journal-title>International Journal of Emergency Medicine</journal-title></journal-title-group><issn pub-type="ppub">1865-1372</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1865-1380</issn><publisher><publisher-name>Springer-Verlag</publisher-name><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">20157458</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2700233</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="publisher-id">99</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s12245-009-0099-6</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Clinical Images</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Ovarian torsion in a prepubertal girl</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author" corresp="yes"><name><surname>Kloss</surname><given-names>Brian T.</given-names></name><address><phone>+201-317-5014</phone><fax>+315-464-6229</fax><email>klossb@upstate.edu</email><email>klossy007@aol.com</email></address><xref ref-type="aff" rid="Aff1">1</xref><xref ref-type="aff" rid="Aff2">2</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Prince</surname><given-names>Louise A.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="Aff1">1</xref></contrib><aff id="Aff1"><label>1</label>The Department of Emergency Medicine, The State University of New York, Upstate Medical University, Syracuse, NY USA </aff><aff id="Aff2"><label>2</label>Department of Emergency Medicine, SUNY Upstate Medical University, 750 East Adams St, Syracuse, NY 13210 USA </aff></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="epub"><day>24</day><month>3</month><year>2009</year></pub-date><pub-date pub-type="pmc-release"><day>24</day><month>3</month><year>2009</year></pub-date><pub-date pub-type="collection"><month>6</month><year>2009</year></pub-date><volume>2</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>127</fpage><lpage>128</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>21</day><month>12</month><year>2008</year></date><date date-type="accepted"><day>17</day><month>2</month><year>2009</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>&#x000a9; Springer-Verlag London Ltd 2009</copyright-statement></permissions><custom-meta-group><custom-meta><meta-name>issue-copyright-statement</meta-name><meta-value>&#x000a9; Springer-Verlag London Ltd 2009</meta-value></custom-meta></custom-meta-group></article-meta></front><body><p>A previously healthy 4-year-old female presented to the Emergency Department complaining of sudden-onset right-lower-quadrant abdominal pain that awoke her from sleep. The pain was constant, non-radiating and severe. She denied trauma, dysuria, hematuria, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, constipation or hematochezia. Her vitals were HR: 92, RR: 16, BP: 116/76 and T: 37.0 &#x000b0;C. Physical exam revealed tenderness at McBurney&#x02019;s point, but no rebound, rigidity or guarding. CBC with differential, basic metabolic panel and urinalysis were all unremarkable. A CT abdomen with contrast and ultrasound revealed a 5.0&#x02009;&#x000d7;&#x02009;4.2&#x02009;&#x000d7;&#x02009;4.8-cm non-communicating cystic mass abutting the left dome of the bladder. The differential diagnosis included mesenteric cyst, enteric duplication cyst, urachal cyst and ovarian cyst. Surgical exploration confirmed the diagnosis of right ovarian cyst with torsion. Kokoska et al. reviewed 51 cases of ovarian torsion between 1983 and 1999 and reported the mean age to be 12.5 &#x000b1; 1.3&#x000a0;years [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="CR1">1</xref>]. A similar study by Anders et al. reviewed 22 cases and calculated the mean age to be 10.2&#x000a0;years with a range of 3&#x02013;15&#x000a0;years [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="CR2">2</xref>]. Ovarian torsion is a rare, but important cause of abdominal pain in younger children that requires a high index of suspicion (Figs. <xref rid="Fig1" ref-type="fig">1</xref>, <xref rid="Fig2" ref-type="fig">2</xref> and <xref rid="Fig3" ref-type="fig">3</xref>).<fig id="Fig1"><label>Fig.&#x000a0;1</label><caption><p>Transverse CT image</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="12245_2009_99_Fig1_HTML" id="MO1"/></fig><fig id="Fig2"><label>Fig.&#x000a0;2</label><caption><p>Coronal CT image</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="12245_2009_99_Fig2_HTML" id="MO2"/></fig><fig id="Fig3"><label>Fig.&#x000a0;3</label><caption><p>Abdominal US image</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="12245_2009_99_Fig3_HTML" id="MO3"/></fig></p></body><back><ref-list id="Bib1"><title>References</title><ref id="CR1"><label>1.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kokoska</surname><given-names>ER</given-names></name><name><surname>Keller</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Wever</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acute ovarian torsion in children</article-title><source>Am J Surg</source><year>2000</year><volume>180</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>462</fpage><lpage>465</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0002-9610(00)00503-1</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11182398</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR2"><label>2.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anders</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Powell</surname><given-names>EC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Urgency of evaluation and outcome of acute ovarian torsion in pediatric patients</article-title><source>Arch Pediatr Adolesc Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>159</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>532</fpage><lpage>535</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/archpedi.159.6.532</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15939851</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>